Subject: chimera: a level's end that waits for a sound keeps its draws

A level does not end while a sound plays: the game goes on ticking, the
timer runs and the torches go on drawing random numbers. SDLPoP
(USE_REPLAY) then puts the seed back to its value on the level's last
tick, so that such a wait shifts nothing. The DOS game keeps what was
drawn. Measured there: the published level 7 line with the sound on
enters level 8 two draws later per tick waited, and level 7 ended with a
closing gate still creaking draws its two torches once more before the
cutscene begins.

Under CHIMERA_CORE the seed is kept.

(Not changed, because the DOS game does the same: with the sound switched
off its sounds still play, silently, for their whole length, and count as
playing - Prince of Persia 1.4, check_sound_playing at 1497:6524 ORs the
"playing" words of its three sound kinds whatever the switch says.)

--- a/src/seg003.c
+++ b/src/seg003.c
@@ -423,7 +423,10 @@
 
 				#ifdef USE_REPLAY
 				if (keep_last_seed == -1) {
+#ifndef CHIMERA_CORE
+					// (the DOS game keeps what the wait for a sound drew)
 					random_seed = preserved_seed; // Ensure reproducibility in the next level.
+#endif
 					keep_last_seed = 0;
 				}
 				#endif
